Package: waydroid-manager
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Felipe Santo <felipeoes@hotmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: waydroid, lxc, dnsmasq-base | dnsmasq, iproute2, iptables | nftables, dbus, systemd,
 python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, python3-cairo, python3-gbinder, libglibutil (>= 1.0.52),
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-rsvg-2.0, gir1.2-pango-1.0
Conflicts: waydroid-multi
Replaces: waydroid-multi
Recommends: wl-clipboard, pkexec | policykit-1
Homepage: https://github.com/felipeoes/waydroid-multi-instances
Description: run several Waydroid (Android) instances side by side
 waydroid-manager runs multiple Android instances at the same time with Waydroid,
 like BlueStacks or LDPlayer multi-instance. Each instance has its own apps,
 accounts, settings, window, network address and resource limits. Instances
 can be created fresh or cloned (with a new device identity). Stock Waydroid
 keeps working unchanged.
 .
 Includes a root daemon, the waydroid-manager command and a GTK manager app.
